          %p A collection of more recent developments is in
          %ul
            %li#vdGeer05
              van der Geer et al (eds.)
              = succeed "," do
                %em Number Fields and Function Fields – Two Parallel Worlds
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.springer.com/birkhauser/mathematics/book/978-0-8176-4397-3"} publisher page
          %p Discussion including also the complex-analytic side includes
          %ul
            %li#Frenkel05
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Frenkel"}> Edward Frenkel
              , section 2 of
              %em Lectures on the Langlands Program and Conformal Field Theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0512172"}> arXiv:hep-th/0512172
              ).
          %p
            and a comparison of the number theory to that of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foliations"} foliations
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Deninger07
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christopher+Deninger"}> Christopher Deninger
              ,
              %em Analogies between analysis on foliated spaces and arithmetic geometry
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0709.2801"}> arXiv:0709.2801
              )
          %p An actual formalization of the analogy between geometry over number fields and function fields is in
          %ul
            %li#Borger09
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Borger"}> James Borger
              , section 7 of
              %em Lambda-rings and the field with one element
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0906.3146"}> arXiv/0906.3146
              )
        .revisedby
